<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">All-Russian Central Executive Committee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The All-Russian Central Executive Committee was the standing body of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-russian-congress-of-soviets">All-Russian Congress of Soviets</a>, exercising legislative power between its sessions from 1917 to 1937. Chaired briefly by Lev Kamenev, then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yakov-sverdlov">Yakov Sverdlov</a> and, from 1919, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-kalinin">Mikhail Kalinin</a>, it was formally the highest organ of the Russian Soviet Republic, although real power lay with the Communist Party.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/all-russian-central-executive-committee.jpg" alt="All-Russian Central Executive Committee" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeromi Mikhael · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Russian_Soviet_Federative_Socialist_Republic_(1920%E2%80%931954).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
